{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"412","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Pattern"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Developers often face with regular expression patterns. A pattern is usually defined as a string consisting of characters and metacharacters that sets the rules for your search. These patterns are most often used to check whether a particular string meets the certain rules."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this task, a pattern will be a string consisting of small English letters and question marks ('"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'). The question mark in the pattern is a metacharacter that denotes an arbitrary small letter of the English alphabet. We will assume that a string matches the pattern if we can transform the string into the pattern by replacing the question marks by the appropriate characters. For example, string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" matches patterns: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"???"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"??a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a?a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Programmers that work for the R1 company love puzzling each other (and themselves) with riddles. One of them is as follows: you are given "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" patterns of the same length, you need to find a pattern that contains as few question marks as possible, and intersects with each of the given patterns. Two patterns intersect if there is a string that matches both the first and the second pattern. Can you solve this riddle?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of patterns. Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the patterns."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the patterns can only consist of small English letters and symbols '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. All patterns are non-empty and have the same length. The total length of all the patterns does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print the answer to the problem — the pattern with the minimal number of signs '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', which intersects with each of the given ones. If there are several answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n?ab\n??b\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"xab\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\na\nb\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"?\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n?a?b\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"cacb\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first example. Pattern "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" intersects with each of the given patterns. Pattern "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"???"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" also intersects with each of the given patterns, but it contains more question signs, hence it is not an optimal answer. Clearly, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the optimal answer, because it doesn't contain any question sign. There are a lot of other optimal answers, for example: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and so on."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"412C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/412/problem/C"}